## Going multi-org (`ARCHITECTURE=multi-org`)

Five moves, all with SDK pieces vibe-starter already imports — the full
version is `providers/index.tsx` in [iblai/os](https://github.com/iblai/os):

1. **Org in the URL** — `app/platform/[tenantKey]/…`; read it with
   `useParams()`; keep `resolveAppTenant()` for the default org.
2. **Providers** — `TenantProvider currentTenant={stored} requestedTenant={fromRoute}`
   with `saveUserTokens`, `saveUserTenants`, `saveCurrentTenant`, `saveTenant`
   implemented (the starter's `iblai-providers.tsx` already has them).
3. **Switching** — `UserProfileDropdown showTenantSwitcher` (or `TenantSwitcher`)
   → `handleTenantSwitch(org, { authUrl })` from `@iblai/iblai-js/web-utils`:
   clears storage, re-enters the SPA with `tenant=`, broadcasts to other tabs.
4. **Anonymous per agent** — in `AuthProvider`'s `middleware`, for
   `^/platform/([^/]+)/([^/]+)` fetch the agent's public settings
   (`useLazyGetMentorPublicSettingsQuery`) and return `false` when
   `allow_anonymous` or `mentor_visibility === "viewable_by_anyone"`.
5. **Landing path guard** — after SSO, reset to `/` when the stored path
   names an org other than the one just authenticated
   (`resolveRedirectPath` on `SsoLogin`).

Register every deployed origin as an allowed redirect origin, exactly as for
a single-org app.